       "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
       "markdown": "Peptides are `short chains of amino acids that act as the building blocks for vital skin proteins like collagen, elastin, and keratin`.[[1]](https://www.boots.com/inspire-me/skincare-advice/ingredients/how-to-use-peptides-in-skincare)[[2]](https://www.paulaschoice.co.uk/what-are-peptides-and-what-do-they-do-for-your-skin)\n\n### What Peptides Do\n\n- **Signal Peptides:** Send messages to skin cells to trigger the production of new collagen and repair visible damage.\n- **Carrier Peptides:** Deliver essential trace elements like copper to the skin to support wound healing and reduce inflammation.\n- **Neurotransmitter Inhibitor Peptides:** Relax facial expression muscles to temporarily smooth out dynamic wrinkles, offering a mild, topical effect similar to cosmetic injections.\n- **Enzyme Inhibitor Peptides:** Slow down the natural breakdown of existing collagen in the skin.[[1]](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11762834/)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WyWDBJIm6wY&t=98)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T4x-Vgax6iQ&t=91)[[4]](https://www.medik8.com/pages/different-types-of-peptides-in-skincare-what-they-do)\n\n### Popular Types and Benefits\n\n- **Matrixyl (3000 or Synthe'6):** Great for boosting overall firmness and reducing the look of fine lines.\n- **Copper Peptides (GHK-Cu):** Exceptional for skin repair, soothing inflammation, and improving overall resilience.\n- **Argireline (Acetyl Hexapeptide-8):** Targeted at expression lines around the forehead and eyes.[[1]](https://www.medik8.com/pages/different-types-of-peptides-in-skincare-what-they-do)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T4x-Vgax6iQ&t=91)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WyWDBJIm6wY&t=98)[[4]](https://www.google.com/search?q=product&prds=pvt:hg,productid:10542029218380412838,catalogid:540920059023938909,gpcid:10969510345251461226,mid:576462334359202436&ibp=oshop)\n\nYou can learn more about how these work from the [Boots Skincare Advice Guide](https://www.boots.com/inspire-me/skincare-advice/ingredients/how-to-use-peptides-in-skincare) . For product formulations and routine tips, see the [The Ordinary Essential Guide to Peptides](https://theordinary.com/en-gb/blog/peptides-skincare-essential-guide.html).[[1]](https://www.boots.com/inspire-me/skincare-advice/ingredients/how-to-use-peptides-in-skincare)[[2]](https://theordinary.com/en-gb/blog/peptides-skincare-essential-guide.html)If you'd like, tell me:\n\n- Your main **skin concern** (aging, redness, firmness)\n- Your **current skincare routine** \n\nI can help you choose the right peptide product to match your goals.",
